	A monster which can't see you is willing to spend its turn
picking stuff up instead of moving.  This can be used against both
nymphs and the Titan.

	For nymphs, have strength 16+ (= you can throw daggers 16/2
= 8 squares).  Dig out a tunnel so that you're standing 8 squares 
from the nymph.  Be as fast or faster than the nymph.  Now throw
daggers.

	The nymph can't see you, and starts every turn with at least
one dagger on the floor in her square.  She will pick up the daggers
until you kill her.

	(Barring trivial problems like not being able to finish her
off before you run out of daggers, having a second monster show up
and chew your arm off, or just stand between you and the nymph, the
nymph waking up while you're still tunnelling....  You know, the usual
YASD trivia.)
 
	For the Titan, I read a scroll of earth without moving off
the stairs.  The Titan can no longer see me and will not summon.  I
start plinking him with daggers ASAP:  Titans can pick up boulders, 
so I have to take him out before he closes.  With luck, the gremlin
doesn't block too many shots.

	This approach works well enough with nymphs, but is relatively
risky with the Titan.  Out of the last three attempts, I had two
successes and one failure (IIRC, I died).  In one case, a Barbarian 
ran through all 12 of his daggers without killing the Titan, which
forced a long pause.

